-- @@ comment VIEW public.ottoq_vehicle_needs_card
COMMENT ON VIEW public.ottoq_vehicle_needs_card IS E'One row per vehicle: every need dimension (energy / cleanliness / sensor+software / mechanical / operational commitment / items) with a value AND a due/urgency signal, plus must_do_now escalation and whether the work fits before next_deploy_at. Run column is run_id (never sim_run_id) so ottoq_purge_prior_runs cannot target it.';
-- @@ comment TABLE public.space_conflict_ledger
COMMENT ON TABLE public.space_conflict_ledger IS E'Auditable record of every calendar claim overruled because a vehicle was PHYSICALLY in the space. Deliberately NOT named ottoq_* so ottoq_purge_prior_runs (which purges every public.ottoq% table carrying sim_run_id) cannot erase the audit trail. Turns "zero double-bookings" from a claim about writes the guard prevented into a measurement of displacements that were recorded.';
-- @@ comment VIEW public.calendar_ledger_integrity
COMMENT ON VIEW public.calendar_ledger_integrity IS E'One definition of booking-to-decision backing. is_phantom = an otto_q_enacted booking with no decision behind it by key (decision_id), by provenance (source), or by inference (vehicle+stall enacted decision). Deliberately not named ottoq_* so ottoq_purge_prior_runs does not attempt to DELETE FROM it.';
-- @@ comment TABLE public.ottoq_cuopt_deferrals
COMMENT ON TABLE public.ottoq_cuopt_deferrals IS E'P2 right-of-first-refusal: one-decide-tick hold so an in-flight cuOpt proposal is not pre-empted by the local greedy path. Named ottoq_* on purpose so ottoq_purge_prior_runs reclaims it with the run. NOT an evidence table.';
-- @@ comment VIEW public.ottoq_indepot_gate_latency
COMMENT ON VIEW public.ottoq_indepot_gate_latency IS E'In-depot reassignment gate latency, measured strictly within one clock domain. latency_min is NULL and clock_domain is ''unmeasurable'' rather than mixing a SIM requested_at_sim with a REAL decided_at -- the error that produced the bogus 0.01-22.18 sim-min range on run 093c20f4. Do not compute gate latency any other way.';
-- @@ comment TABLE public.ottoq_retention_policy
